

Sleeping during your period can sometimes feel difficult, especially when your menstrual flow is heavy. Worrying about leaks can make it harder to relax and get proper sleep.

The good news is that choosing the right menstrual product and following a few simple habits can make nighttime periods much easier to manage.

Choose an Overnight Pad

One of the most useful steps is choosing a pad designed for nighttime use.

Overnight pads are generally longer and provide additional front-to-back coverage. This can be helpful because menstrual fluid may move differently while you are lying down.

A longer pad can also provide extra protection if you tend to move around during sleep.

