Position Your Pad Correctly

Before going to bed, make sure the pad is positioned properly in your underwear.

It should be centred comfortably, with the wings securely attached around the sides. If the pad is too far forward or backward, it may not provide the coverage you need.

Consider Your Flow

Your menstrual flow may be heavier during the first few days of your period.

If you experience heavy flow, a regular daytime pad may not provide enough protection overnight. A longer, higher-absorbency product may be a better option.

Choosing the right absorbency can reduce the chances of waking up because of leakage.

Change Your Pad Before Bed

Starting the night with a fresh pad can provide greater comfort.

Change your pad before going to sleep rather than using a product that has already been worn for several hours.

If you wake during the night and notice that your pad is saturated or uncomfortable, change it.

Keep Spare Pads Nearby

Keeping a few spare pads next to your bed can be useful. If you need to change during the night, you will not have to search for supplies.

This is particularly useful during the heavier days of your period.

Protect Your Bedding

If you frequently worry about leaks, placing a washable towel or protective layer over your bedsheet can provide extra peace of mind.

Accidental leaks can happen, and they are nothing to feel embarrassed about. Preparing for them can simply make the experience less stressful.

When Should You Consider Medical Advice?

If you regularly soak through your menstrual product during the night, wake repeatedly because of heavy bleeding, or experience extremely heavy periods, consider discussing your symptoms with a healthcare professional.

Heavy menstrual bleeding can sometimes have an underlying cause and should not always be dismissed as normal.

Sleep Comfortably During Your Period

A comfortable nighttime routine can make a big difference. Use a suitable overnight pad, position it correctly, change it before bed, keep spare products nearby, and choose absorbency according to your flow.

